# PHP test/support type hints

**Condition:** every function and every class method in `tests/**/*.php` must declare parameter and return types in the PHP signature. Docblocks (`@param`, `@return`) alone do **not** satisfy static analysis and will still trigger editor warnings such as `Parameter $key has no type information available`.

This applies to:

- top-level helper functions (`function mtuc_assert(...)`)
- stub/harness classes declared inside check scripts (`class Phase1InstallHarness`)
- support files under `tests/support/`

## Floor

- Target PHP **7.3.0+** (see `docs/CONTRACTS.md` D1).
- Allowed: `bool`, `int`, `float`, `string`, `array`, `void`, class names, `?T` nullable (PHP 7.1+).
- Avoid PHP 7.4+ only syntax in signatures: typed properties, union types, `mixed`, constructor promotion.

## Examples

```php
// BAD — analyzer: "Parameter has no type information available"
function mtuc_assert($condition, $message) { }

class Phase1InstallHarness {
    public function insertDefault($key, $value, $storeId = 0) { }
}

// GOOD
function mtuc_assert(bool $condition, string $message): void { }

class Phase1InstallHarness {
    public function getSettingValue(string $key, int $storeId = 0): ?string { }

    public function insertDefault(string $key, string $value, int $storeId = 0): void { }

    public function getInsertCount(): int { }
}

function mtuc_phase0_load_fixture(string $name): array { }

function mtuc_phase0_contains_live_remote_host(string $contents): bool { }
```

When adding new test helpers or inline harness classes, type every parameter and return value explicitly in the signature.
